 ## Background
-Scalar leaf traversal is part of the interactive isosurface ray tracing of large octree volumes method, introduced by Knoll et al. in 2006. It is designed to handle the leaf nodes of sparse voxel octrees efficiently, allowing for real-time rendering of large volumes. The method builds on the ray-octree traversal technique by Gargantini and Atkinson, adapting it to handle scalar leaves specifically.
